.TH WITH-LOCK 1 "October 2026" "devtools-hub 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
with-lock \- execute a command under an exclusive POSIX atomic mutex lock
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B with-lock
.I lock-name
.I command
.RI [ args... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B with-lock
acquires an exclusive filesystem lock inside
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME
(or
.BR /tmp )
using atomic
.BR mkdir (1)
semantics before executing
.IR command .
It prevents overlapping cron jobs or concurrent CI deployments across Linux, macOS, and BSD environments where
.BR flock (1)
may not be portable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Lock was acquired and the wrapped command exited successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, lock contention detected, or wrapped command failure.
